WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.329
Once upon a time, there lived an old fisherman and his wife.

2
00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:10.952
They lived in a modest hut on a small island.

3
00:00:10.953 --> 00:00:16.039
Every day the fisherman went fishing with his net.

4
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:22.798
Usually he did not catch many fish, but one day his luck changed.

5
00:00:22.799 --> 00:00:28.654
"Oh my!" the fisherman exclaimed as he started to haul in his heavy net.

6
00:00:28.655 --> 00:00:33.057
"I must have caught an enormous fish!"

7
00:00:33.058 --> 00:00:37.765
But when the fisherman looked in the net, he was stunned.

8
00:00:37.766 --> 00:00:44.744
The heavy net was empty, except for one tiny golden fish.

9
00:00:44.745 --> 00:00:48.854
The fisherman peered more closely at the fish.

10
00:00:48.855 --> 00:00:53.452
Suddenly the creature opened its mouth, startling the man.

11
00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:57.708
"Please do not kill me!" the golden fish pleaded.

12
00:00:57.709 --> 00:01:03.039
"Return me to the sea and I will do whatever you wish."

13
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.552
"This is no ordinary fish!" the old man realized.

14
00:01:07.553 --> 00:01:12.920
He took pity on the small creature. "I am content," he said.

15
00:01:12.921 --> 00:01:18.002
"I do not need anything from you. Go back to the sea."

16
00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:24.383
At home the fisherman's wife asked, as she always did, "Did you catch anything today?"

17
00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:29.287
The fisherman shrugged. "Nothing but a small golden fish."

18
00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:34.862
Then the fisherman told his wife about the extraordinary golden fish in his net.

19
00:01:34.863 --> 00:01:41.921
When the man relayed that he had let the golden fish go, his wife's face darkened with fury.

20
00:01:41.922 --> 00:01:48.924
"You fool!" she bellowed. "That was a magic fish! Why did you let it go?

21
00:01:48.925 --> 00:01:53.664
Why did you not wish for something—like bread for us to eat?"

22
00:01:53.665 --> 00:01:58.305
The wife reprimanded her husband all night long.

23
00:01:58.306 --> 00:02:03.202
Finally the fisherman couldn't stand his wife's complaints anymore.

24
00:02:03.203 --> 00:02:07.214
He returned to the sea to look for the magic fish.

25
00:02:07.215 --> 00:02:12.569
"Little fish, little fish," the man called out.

26
00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:19.408
Soon the golden fish swam to the shore. "What do you want, old man?"

27
00:02:19.409 --> 00:02:23.713
"My wife is very angry," the fisherman said.

28
00:02:23.714 --> 00:02:26.602
"She wants me to ask you for something."

29
00:02:26.603 --> 00:02:30.339
"What does she want?" asked the fish.

30
00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.899
"She wants bread," replied the man.

31
00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:37.569
"You gave me my life," answered the fish.

32
00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:44.383
"Go home and you will find what your wife wished for." Then it swam away.

33
00:02:44.384 --> 00:02:50.202
When the man returned to his hut, he asked, "Do we have bread now?"

34
00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:55.570
"We have plenty of bread now," his wife informed him.

35
00:02:55.571 --> 00:03:00.150
"But our hut is in disrepair and about to collapse!

36
00:03:00.151 --> 00:03:06.232
Return to the golden fish and demand a fine new cottage!"

37
00:03:06.233 --> 00:03:11.764
"Little fish, little fish," the man called out.

38
00:03:11.765 --> 00:03:18.316
Soon the golden fish swam to the shore. "What do you want, old man?"

39
00:03:18.317 --> 00:03:25.124
"My wife is discontent. Now she wants a fine new cottage," the man answered.

40
00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:32.690
"Go home and you will find what she wished for," said the fish. Then it swam away.

41
00:03:32.691 --> 00:03:42.059
When the man returned home, he was amazed to see that a fine new cottage had replaced his small, modest hut.

42
00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:45.571
Just then, his wife ran toward him.

43
00:03:45.572 --> 00:03:49.406
"Go back to the golden fish!" she demanded.

44
00:03:49.407 --> 00:03:54.639
"And tell the fish I want to be queen of this island!"

45
00:03:54.640 --> 00:04:00.196
Again the fisherman obeyed his wife's command and headed back to the sea.

46
00:04:00.197 --> 00:04:05.093
"Little fish, little fish," he called out.

47
00:04:05.094 --> 00:04:13.226
Soon the golden fish swam to the shore. "What do you want now, old man?"

48
00:04:13.227 --> 00:04:17.250
"My wife wants to be the queen of the island."

49
00:04:17.251 --> 00:04:25.597
"Go home and you will find what she wished for," said the fish. Then it swam away.

50
00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:31.722
When the fisherman arrived home, he stopped in his tracks and stared in amazement.

51
00:04:31.723 --> 00:04:39.483
A magnificent palace, bustling with guards, horses, and servants, had replaced the cottage!

52
00:04:39.484 --> 00:04:49.979
The old man entered the palace. Sitting on a golden throne, dressed in the elegant attire of a queen, was his wife.

53
00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:54.834
"Pardon me, wife?" The man spoke quietly.

54
00:04:54.835 --> 00:05:04.506
"Wife? How dare you address the queen as your wife!" she screamed loudly. "Guards! Take this disgusting man away!"

55
00:05:04.507 --> 00:05:15.551
The guards dragged the fisherman away. While his wife ruled the island, he spent his days sweeping the palace like a servant.

56
00:05:15.552 --> 00:05:23.812
Then one day the queen summoned the fisherman. "You old fool!" she ordered him.

57
00:05:23.813 --> 00:05:28.600
"Go back to that fish and tell him that I no longer want to be queen.

58
00:05:28.601 --> 00:05:33.204
Now I want to be the empress of the sea!"

59
00:05:33.205 --> 00:05:38.162
"What?" The man stared at his greedy wife in disbelief.

60
00:05:38.163 --> 00:05:42.589
"No," he refused, slowly shaking his head.

61
00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:47.934
"You already have more than you need."

62
00:05:47.935 --> 00:05:53.564
"Go to the fish or I will chop your head off!" threatened the queen.

63
00:05:53.565 --> 00:06:00.220
The fisherman was taken back to the sea. "Little fish, little fish."

64
00:06:00.221 --> 00:06:04.257
But this time the golden fish did not appear.

65
00:06:04.258 --> 00:06:09.331
"Little fish, little fish," the man called again.

66
00:06:09.332 --> 00:06:13.026
Still the golden fish did not answer.

67
00:06:13.027 --> 00:06:19.749
The old man called out a third time, "Little fish, little fish."

68
00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:27.070
Suddenly the sky turned dark and the waves in the sea crashed and roared.

69
00:06:27.071 --> 00:06:31.369
At last the golden fish swam up to the shore.

70
00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:34.475
"What do you want, old man?"

71
00:06:34.476 --> 00:06:39.568
The fisherman bent his head low and spoke in a trembling voice.

72
00:06:39.569 --> 00:06:46.511
"My . . . my wife . . . now she . . . wants to be the empress of the sea."

73
00:06:46.512 --> 00:06:50.242
The fish did not say a word.

74
00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:56.525
Instead it simply turned and disappeared into the churning waters.

75
00:06:56.526 --> 00:07:01.532
When the old man returned home, he could not believe his eyes.

76
00:07:01.533 --> 00:07:08.389
The magnificent palace was gone. In its place stood their old modest hut.

77
00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:12.749
The fisherman and his wife returned to their former life.

78
00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:17.170
Every day the fisherman went fishing, as usual.

79
00:07:17.171 --> 00:07:25.468
But he never caught the extraordinary golden fish again.

